---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Block from "../components/Block.astro";
import Img from "../components/Img.astro";
import Marquee from "../components/Marquee.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Protect Your Privacy Today" description="Jeff Humble's Privacy Policy details how your data is handled, protected, and used responsibly, ensuring transparency and privacy rights adherence.">
  <Section theme="white" height={15} rows={{ mobile: 4, desktop: 5, scale: 0.0215 }}>
    <Block m="1/1/5/11" d="1/1/6/27" z={1} valignM="middle" valign="top">
      <Marquee h1 items={["Privacy Policy"]} textStyle="heading-1" speed={0.5} direction="left" size={8} />
    </Block>

    <Block m="1/1/2/11" d="5/1/6/27" z={4}>
      <hr />
    </Block>

    <Block m="4/1/5/11" d="1/1/2/27" z={3} valignM="middle" valign="bottom">
      <hr />
    </Block>
  </Section>

  <Section theme="white" height="medium" rows={{ mobile: 81, desktop: 46, scale: 0.0215 }}>
    <Block m="1/2/76/10" d="1/8/47/20" z={2} valign="top">
      <div class="rich text-block">
        <p class="text-large">In simple words:</p><ul><li><p class="text-large">Jeff will NEVER sell your Personal Data to Third Parties. </p></li><li><p class="text-large">Jeff will be educational, not annoying.</p></li><li><p class="text-large">Jeff will make it easy to opt out of our communications.</p></li></ul><p>This Privacy Policy applies to Personal Data processed by Jeff Humble (“Jeff Humble”, “We”, “Us” and “Our”) when You visit www.jeffreyhumble.com in addition to any sub-pages that are integrated within it (the “Site”); and make use of Jeff Humble’s learning experiences.</p><p>This Privacy Policy explains what Personal Data We collect through Our Site and Software, how and why We collect it, how We use and disclose it, and information on how to exercise privacy rights over this Personal Data.</p><p>These Terms of Use govern participation in courses, workshops, events, community interactions from Jeff Humble, and how we process viewers’ and subscribers' personal data.<br/><br/>Jeff Humble collects the following types of personal information from users:</p><ol><li><p>Contact information, such as name, email address, and telephone number.</p></li><li><p>Demographic information, such as age, gender, and location.</p></li><li><p>Information about your use of our services, such as the pages you visit and the actions you take.</p></li><li><p>Any other information you choose to provide to us, such as feedback or survey responses.</p></li></ol><p>We may collect personal information through various means, including:</p><ol><li><p>Directly from you, when you provide information through our website, services, or when you contact us directly.</p></li><li><p>Automatically, through the use of technologies such as cookies and web beacons, when you use our website or services.</p></li></ol><h3>Use of Personal Information</h3><p>Jeff Humble uses your personal information for the following purposes:</p><ol><li><p>To provide and improve his services, including customizing your experience with our website and services.</p></li><li><p>Communicate with you, such as responding to your inquiries or sending updates on our services.</p></li><li><p>To perform research and analysis, such as tracking usage patterns and gathering demographic information.</p></li><li><p>To comply with legal obligations, such as responding to subpoenas or court orders.</p></li></ol><h3>Data Sharing and Disclosure</h3><p>Jeff Humble does not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for their own marketing purposes. We may share your personal information with third parties for the following purposes:</p><ol><li><p>To provide and improve our services, such as sharing information with service providers who assist us with website hosting, data analysis, and customer support.</p></li><li><p>To comply with legal obligations, such as disclosing information to law enforcement or other government agencies in response to a subpoena or court order.</p></li></ol><h3>Why we collect your data</h3><ul><li><p>To process your application and conclude a request for work</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>To send you a newsletter or educational email (coming soon)</p></li><li><p>To inform you about offers that from Jeff Humble</p></li></ul><h3>Protection of Personal Information</h3><p>Jeff Humble takes the protection of personal information very seriously and implements appropriate security measures to protect against unauthorized access, use, alteration, or destruction of your personal information. We use industry-standard encryption and secure storage to protect your data and regularly monitor our systems for security breaches.</p><h3>Data Retention</h3><p>Jeff Humble retains limited personal information for as long as it is necessary to provide our services and for the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy. We may retain certain data for longer periods if required by law or for our legitimate business purposes.</p>
      </div>
    </Block>

    <Block m="76/2/82/10" d="1/20/7/26" z={3}>
      <Img src="/images/0abea284-ab6d-431d-8ae9-d17e9bb72807/Surfing_computer_guy.png" alt="A man in a business suit stands on a computer keyboard with arms extended outward, as if balancing or preparing to jump." fit="contain" width={299} height={365} />
    </Block>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
